@startuml piece_promotion
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' piece_promotion — v28.9, where a piece's minutes are counted.
'
' The picture to hold: ONE trigger, the DATE. A dated piece receives its
' own verdict from affordability's first guard, so its minutes leave the
' parent — whichever path the parent is on (own estimate: subtract;
' borrowing: skip). The believed total always equals what was entered,
' once. Referenced from design-addendum-subtasks.md §O.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

start
:a piece, with an estimate;
if (has its own due date?) then (yes — PROMOTED)
  :answers for ITSELF:
  own verdict, own nudge,
  own needs-a-block line;
  :its minutes LEAVE the parent
  (subtracted from a sized parent,
  skipped by an unsized one's borrow);
else (no)
  :no verdict of its own
  (affordability needs a date);
  :weighs on the parent
  (inside its estimate, or
  borrowed when unsized);
endif
:believed total = entered total, once;
note right
  Floor at zero: pieces promoted
  past the parent's estimate cede
  ALL of it — the parent falls back
  to the planned-blocks proxy,
  never goes negative.
end note
stop
@enduml
